WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.560
Game of Thrones' Gilly has been surprising
us from her first episode, and as the series

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.950
finale and all the battle and bloodshed it
brings with it crests the horizon, she's not

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.700
likely to stop anytime soon.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.900
How might the young woman from Craster's Keep
turn the tide of battle?

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.840
If you're all caught up on your Game of Thrones
binges, then you've probably grown accustomed

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.760
to seeing Gilly embarking on ocean voyages
or in the relative safety of the Citadel.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.400
It might be easy to forget that Gilly spent
most of her life in the dangerous lands beyond

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:28.900
the Wall.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.860
She knows the North like only a wildling could,
and she holds no illusions about how desperate

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:34.960
life there can be.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:41.000
While season 7 ended with the Walkers shattering
the Wall in a spectacular burst of blue dragonfire,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.600
it seems likely that at least part of the
final season could take place in the far North

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.800
and Gilly could prove a unique guide to those
frozen and forbidding lands.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.239
Not to mention that while most of Game of
Thrones' central characters have until now

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:58.969
seen the White Walkers as nothing more than
some laughable child's tale, Gilly grew up

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:01.100
with the Walkers as an absolute certainty.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.720
They were a part of her daily life.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.300
As one of Craster's wives, the Walkers' appetites
defined her life and she understands them

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.040
as few can.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:15.000
In the season 7 finale, one of the most popular
fan theories was confirmed by Bran Stark and

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.880
his psychic, time-spanning visions.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.000
It turns out that Jon Snow isn't a bastard
at all, but the child of Rhaegar Targaryen

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.880
and Lyanna Stark.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.240
Which means that Daenerys isn't the last Targaryen
and that Jon is the true heir to the Iron

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:28.740
Throne.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.480
But before Bran peeled back the layers of
time and space, there was Gilly, discovering

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.460
it in a forgotten journal, buried in the bowels
of the Citadel.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.440
In the season 7 episode "Eastwatch," as she
and Sam pored over the spoils of the Citadel's

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:47.220
library, Gilly found a description of an annulment
granted to Jon Snow's true father.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.900
"Maynard says here that he issued an annulment
for a Prince Ragnard, and remarried him to

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.860
someone else at the same time."

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.380
Not only was she the first person to stumble
onto this explosive fact, she is now one of

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.820
the few people who knows it at all.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.480
In a sense, the moment Gilly discovered it,
she became one of the most dangerous people

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.120
in Westeros.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:09.580
"Gilly…"

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:16.740
"I worry about you."

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.060
Regardless of his noble birth, Sam was never
going to be the heir to Horn Hill.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.720
He's a sensitive and scholarly man who doesn't
live up to his father's narrow standards.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.740
Sam is no longer part of House Tarly, having
forsworn his claim for the Night's Watch and

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.680
disowned by his tyrant of a father.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.420
Since Sam's father and brother Dickon were
executed by Daenerys for refusing to bend

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.420
the knee, technically Sam's sister Talla is
now the heir and the Lady of Horn Hill.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:47.260
But let's be honest: the letter of the law
doesn't count for much in Westeros.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.980
What matters is who shows up, who fights the
hardest, and who has something to show for

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.480
it.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.400
He may be quiet and bookish; but Sam has killed
a White Walker, smuggled royals across Kingdom

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.920
lines, sworn to protect Gilly and her child,
and helped uncover a decades-old secret.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.200
“He drove a dagger into the walkers heart.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.860
He’s risked his own life to save mine more
than once.”

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.120
"He's a greater warrior than either of you
will ever be."

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Sam absolutely could end up as the Lord of
Horn Hill.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:15.960
And if he did?

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.780
That would make Gilly his Lady, and baby Sam
the heir.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:23.900
Horn Hill is fabulous even by the standards
of noble houses, and has been cozy with other

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.640
families of the Reach for decades.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:30.000
This wouldn't just be an incredible place
of power for an abused Wildling girl, but

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.140
an incredible place of power, period.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.640
Few Game of Thrones characters have traveled
as far as Gilly.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.400
She began in the fearsome world north of the
Wall, where she shared her home with massive

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.440
giants and the growing army of the dead.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.040
She spent time at Castle Black, where she
made a home among her enemies.

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:50.689
Gilly has feasted in the opulent halls of
Horn Hill, learned to read in the legendary

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:54.960
Citadel, and is now in residence at Winterfell
alongside the reunited remnants of the Stark

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:55.460
family.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.840
Few characters in Game of Thrones especially
commoners have been as far or has met so many

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.700
powerful people.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:06.920
Gilly has connections to the common folk of
Westeros as well as the greatest noble houses.

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:11.779
She may have begun as a simple Wildling girl,
but now she's the maypole around which multiple

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.760
ribbons of plot and character are wound.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.440
The show's final season will reveal which
ribbon tugs the strongest.

